WEBVTT

﻿1
00:00:32.993 --> 00:00:36.162
The last time I spent this long in bed,
was because I strained a hamstring.

2
00:00:48.967 --> 00:00:50.260
Should we…

3
00:00:51.720 --> 00:00:52.929
tell people about us?

4
00:00:55.807 --> 00:00:57.517
I'm enjoying the secrecy.

5
00:00:59.477 --> 00:01:01.396
Sneaking around at work.

6
00:01:03.064 --> 00:01:05.609
Doesn't it feel scandalous and fun?

7
00:01:05.692 --> 00:01:09.321
No. It's so stressful.

8
00:01:09.404 --> 00:01:10.947
I'm going gray.

9
00:01:11.031 --> 00:01:13.700
I have not seen one gray hair anywhere.

10
00:01:13.783 --> 00:01:15.035
It's not on my head.

11
00:01:16.661 --> 00:01:19.706
It's not down there.
It's in my armpits. See?

12
00:01:22.876 --> 00:01:24.294
Problem solved.

13
00:01:25.879 --> 00:01:29.382
You know, if we told people about us,

14
00:01:29.466 --> 00:01:31.009
then I could do this…

15
00:01:31.593 --> 00:01:32.594
in public.

16
00:01:33.428 --> 00:01:35.972
You are not gonna
let this one go, are you?

17
00:01:36.056 --> 00:01:37.891
No, I am not.

18
00:01:41.561 --> 00:01:43.104
You know, we have the weekend off.

19
00:01:45.065 --> 00:01:46.233
Then I'm in.

20
00:01:47.567 --> 00:01:49.444
-Where are we going?
-How about Greece?

21
00:01:49.527 --> 00:01:51.071
Oh, my God, Mother!

22
00:01:53.448 --> 00:01:55.575
Excellent,
that's where my spare keys went.

23
00:01:56.159 --> 00:01:57.619
Sam, you remember my mother?

24
00:01:57.702 --> 00:02:00.247
It's a pleasure
to formally meet you, Deborah.

25
00:02:00.330 --> 00:02:02.290
I sincerely wish
I wasn't in my boxers right now.

26
00:02:02.916 --> 00:02:04.084
Boxer briefs.

27
00:02:04.751 --> 00:02:06.336
And like clunky exposition,

28
00:02:06.419 --> 00:02:08.379
they leave very little to the imagination.

29
00:02:08.462 --> 00:02:09.713
I am so sorry.

30
00:02:09.798 --> 00:02:12.676
Right, okay, that's all the pleasantries
out of the way.

31
00:02:12.759 --> 00:02:13.843
So come on, Mother.

32
00:02:14.386 --> 00:02:16.054
What's my father done this time?

33
00:02:17.097 --> 00:02:18.181
He died.

34
00:02:49.462 --> 00:02:52.090
So where do you think
her father is right now?

35
00:02:52.173 --> 00:02:53.842
In the drawer of a funeral home.

36
00:02:53.925 --> 00:02:56.678
No. I mean, like, spiritually.

37
00:02:57.721 --> 00:02:59.347
In the drawer of a funeral home.

38
00:03:00.056 --> 00:03:01.766
You know, growing up,
I used to believe that

39
00:03:01.850 --> 00:03:03.602
if you did good things,
you went to heaven.

40
00:03:03.685 --> 00:03:05.562
You did bad things, you went to hell.

41
00:03:05.645 --> 00:03:09.774
Nowadays, I know we all just do both.
So wherever he is, I hope he's happy.

42
00:03:10.358 --> 00:03:13.403
I like to imagine a heaven
where animals are in charge,

43
00:03:13.486 --> 00:03:14.905
and humans are the pets.

44
00:03:15.906 --> 00:03:18.909
I'd like to spend eternity
curled up in front of a fire

45
00:03:19.743 --> 00:03:21.328
at Cindy Clawford's feet.

46
00:03:21.411 --> 00:03:22.537
Yeah.

47
00:03:22.621 --> 00:03:24.664
I'd like to be reincarnated as a tiger…

48
00:03:25.999 --> 00:03:28.209
and then ravage anyone
who looked at me wrong.

49
00:03:30.503 --> 00:03:33.131
You know, if you weigh
a person's body right after death,

50
00:03:33.215 --> 00:03:34.966
it's 21.3 grams lighter,

51
00:03:35.550 --> 00:03:38.345
and some say that's
the weight of the soul.

52
00:03:39.679 --> 00:03:41.473
Whoever figured that out

53
00:03:41.556 --> 00:03:44.726
clearly weighed someone,
murdered them, then weighed them again.

54
00:03:46.144 --> 00:03:48.605
You live, you die, you're done.

55
00:03:48.688 --> 00:03:49.814
Good night.

56
00:03:52.943 --> 00:03:55.612
-He's on his period.
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

57
00:03:57.030 --> 00:04:00.951
Oi, so we're all going
to this funeral as a team.

58
00:04:01.868 --> 00:04:05.997
So that means ties, shirts…

59
00:04:07.290 --> 00:04:09.417
-and no trainers.
-What?

60
00:04:10.835 --> 00:04:11.836
Okay.

61
00:04:11.920 --> 00:04:13.838
Well, what if they're,
like, really nice Yeezys?

62
00:04:13.922 --> 00:04:15.840
-Yeah.
-What color?

63
00:04:17.550 --> 00:04:18.634
Bright red.

64
00:04:21.680 --> 00:04:23.723
Okay, I'll wear some dress shoes.

65
00:04:24.808 --> 00:04:26.268
Where do you get dress shoes?

66
00:04:26.351 --> 00:04:28.186
I don't have time to stand
in line at midnight

67
00:04:28.270 --> 00:04:30.063
and wait till morning to buy new shoes.

68
00:04:30.146 --> 00:04:32.524
You don't have to do that
for shoes like these, mate.

69
00:04:32.607 --> 00:04:33.984
Nobody wants them.

70
00:04:47.747 --> 00:04:50.959
Oh, my God! This fucking song!

71
00:04:51.543 --> 00:04:53.503
Mother, turn it off!

72
00:04:54.379 --> 00:04:56.089
Hang on! Hang on, sausage.

73
00:04:56.172 --> 00:04:57.173
I can't hear you.

74
00:04:57.257 --> 00:04:59.301
Of course you can't fucking hear me.

75
00:05:00.719 --> 00:05:02.971
-What did you want?
-Why are you playing that song?

76
00:05:03.054 --> 00:05:06.725
I'm sorry. I like to have it playing
in every room in the house when I wake up.

77
00:05:06.808 --> 00:05:08.351
It just makes me feel happy.

78
00:05:08.435 --> 00:05:11.146
Well, you shouldn't feel happy today.

79
00:05:11.229 --> 00:05:13.440
You should feel happy every day, Rebecca.

80
00:05:13.523 --> 00:05:14.774
Do you want to talk about that?

81
00:05:15.567 --> 00:05:17.360
No-- I am happy.

82
00:05:17.444 --> 00:05:19.613
I don't need to talk about anything.

83
00:05:20.196 --> 00:05:22.741
You know, the old Rebecca
used to love that song.

84
00:05:22.824 --> 00:05:24.868
Yeah, well,
the whole world used to love that song.

85
00:05:24.951 --> 00:05:27.829
Then we heard it ad nauseam,
and now we're over it.

86
00:05:27.913 --> 00:05:29.789
Well, I don't work that way.

87
00:05:29.873 --> 00:05:31.917
Once I love something, I love it forever.

88
00:05:35.545 --> 00:05:37.964
You know, you can change this room
to whatever you want.

89
00:05:38.882 --> 00:05:40.634
You don't need to keep it
like this for me.

90
00:05:42.177 --> 00:05:45.555
No, it reminds me of when we were close.

91
00:05:45.639 --> 00:05:47.432
I want it that way.

92
00:05:48.808 --> 00:05:50.393
Now I know what song I want to play next.

93
00:05:50.477 --> 00:05:52.395
Oh, no!

94
00:05:52.479 --> 00:05:53.772
Good morning, Stinky.

95
00:05:58.818 --> 00:06:01.238
What the hell are you thinking?

96
00:06:01.321 --> 00:06:02.948
Just wanted to see if I could still do it.

97
00:06:03.448 --> 00:06:06.534
Those Tracy Anderson workouts are having
the right effect.

98
00:06:06.618 --> 00:06:07.994
Nora, hurry up!

99
00:06:08.078 --> 00:06:10.830
I'm taking my time and being careful.

100
00:06:10.914 --> 00:06:13.124
When I was your age,
I could do this in seconds.

101
00:06:13.208 --> 00:06:14.209
That's true.

102
00:06:14.292 --> 00:06:15.585
While drunk, by the way.

103
00:06:15.669 --> 00:06:17.796
Florence, darling, it's been ages.

104
00:06:17.879 --> 00:06:19.881
-Deborah.
-Thank you for coming.

105
00:06:20.799 --> 00:06:23.426
Nora and I are here
for anything you need, okay?

106
00:06:23.510 --> 00:06:24.761
Isn't that right, Nora?

107
00:06:26.012 --> 00:06:27.931
-Nora!
-Oh, God.

108
00:06:30.892 --> 00:06:32.018
I'm okay.

109
00:06:37.607 --> 00:06:39.442
Funerals are weird, aren't they?

110
00:06:39.526 --> 00:06:40.819
Yeah.

111
00:06:40.902 --> 00:06:41.987
Yeah.

112
00:06:43.029 --> 00:06:45.031
They're like a party,

113
00:06:45.115 --> 00:06:46.408
but for sad people.

114
00:06:47.409 --> 00:06:50.161
Like where everyone knows
they have to go and be sad.

115
00:06:51.454 --> 00:06:52.872
Maybe you're not sad,

116
00:06:53.498 --> 00:06:55.166
but you have to go and be sad.

117
00:06:56.251 --> 00:06:57.377
I think that's weird.

118
00:06:57.460 --> 00:06:58.879
Yeah, they're horrible.

119
00:07:01.214 --> 00:07:04.342
Roy, if you die,
do you want to be buried or cremated?

120
00:07:04.426 --> 00:07:06.845
Like, if you were hit by a bus today,
what do I do?

121
00:07:08.013 --> 00:07:11.224
Go after the bus driver
and make him pay for what he did to me.

122
00:07:11.308 --> 00:07:12.893
Avenge me, Keeley.

123
00:07:12.976 --> 00:07:14.436
Avenge me!

124
00:07:16.354 --> 00:07:18.273
This funeral is really messing
with your head, innit?

125
00:07:18.356 --> 00:07:20.025
I found this company,

126
00:07:20.942 --> 00:07:23.904
and they bury you in a biodegradable sack.

127
00:07:23.987 --> 00:07:25.822
So when your body decomposes,

128
00:07:25.906 --> 00:07:28.283
it fertilizes the seeds of a fruit tree.

129
00:07:28.366 --> 00:07:29.659
That's what I want.

130
00:07:29.743 --> 00:07:31.828
Because then you
and all the people that love me

131
00:07:31.912 --> 00:07:33.580
can eat the fruit from my tree.

132
00:07:33.663 --> 00:07:35.290
That is fucking mental.

133
00:07:35.373 --> 00:07:39.002
Coming from the guy
that wants me to ruin a bus driver's life

134
00:07:39.085 --> 00:07:42.214
just 'cause he killed you
swerving to avoid a child.

135
00:07:42.297 --> 00:07:44.299
I didn't know about the fucking child.

136
00:07:46.843 --> 00:07:49.638
I just like the idea
that my death can nourish people.

137
00:07:49.721 --> 00:07:52.015
With fruit made from your rotting corpse?

138
00:07:52.641 --> 00:07:53.934
I wouldn't eat that.

139
00:07:54.851 --> 00:07:57.270
But you'll eat a kebab
that you find a hair in?

140
00:07:57.354 --> 00:07:59.231
It's fine if you know
who the hair is from.

141
00:07:59.314 --> 00:08:01.441
That's part of the deal.
He's a lovely bloke.

142
00:08:03.235 --> 00:08:05.779
-You're not really angry, are you?
-Yes, I actually am.

143
00:08:06.279 --> 00:08:08.949
And now we have to go to
a funeral and act sad.

144
00:08:12.244 --> 00:08:13.370
Well, now I am sad.

145
00:08:57.205 --> 00:08:58.415
Shit.

146
00:09:08.049 --> 00:09:10.093
We're so sorry for your loss.

147
00:09:10.176 --> 00:09:12.929
Oh, my goodness.
I can't believe you made it.

148
00:09:13.013 --> 00:09:15.640
-Of course.
-Dad always loved you both.

149
00:09:19.811 --> 00:09:20.979
Who are they?

150
00:09:21.062 --> 00:09:22.230
I've no idea.

151
00:09:22.898 --> 00:09:24.566
My darling, Deborah.

152
00:09:24.649 --> 00:09:25.692
Rupert.

153
00:09:25.775 --> 00:09:27.819
My sincerest condolences.

154
00:09:29.362 --> 00:09:30.697
Didn't think you were coming.

155
00:09:31.281 --> 00:09:32.824
Rebecca, Paul was family.

156
00:09:32.908 --> 00:09:34.743
No, I mean because you weren't invited.

157
00:09:35.619 --> 00:09:37.704
It's lovely to see you, Rupie.

158
00:09:41.374 --> 00:09:43.209
And introducing Diane.

159
00:09:44.753 --> 00:09:46.296
What a chubby baby.

160
00:09:47.714 --> 00:09:50.675
Congratulations, Mother.
You've just fat-shamed a baby to tears.

161
00:09:50.759 --> 00:09:52.177
Come here.

162
00:09:57.766 --> 00:10:00.560
Et voilà, the magic touch.

163
00:10:00.644 --> 00:10:02.062
It's not magic.

164
00:10:02.145 --> 00:10:05.398
I ate the placenta raw, and she knows it.

165
00:10:07.150 --> 00:10:09.194
Yeah,
I had all the TVs in the house removed.

166
00:10:09.277 --> 00:10:11.196
I just sit around and watch them all day.

167
00:10:11.279 --> 00:10:12.614
How lovely.

168
00:10:12.697 --> 00:10:14.157
Excuse me.

169
00:10:23.083 --> 00:10:24.960
-My condolences.
-Thank you, Leslie.

170
00:10:26.086 --> 00:10:27.337
Sorry, Ms. Welton.

171
00:10:29.756 --> 00:10:30.840
Sorry for your loss.

172
00:10:30.924 --> 00:10:33.385
-How many of them came?
-All of them.

173
00:10:37.764 --> 00:10:40.058
And none of them are wearing trainers.

174
00:10:40.141 --> 00:10:41.810
That's how much they care about you.

175
00:10:43.687 --> 00:10:46.815
-My feet are killing me, man.
-We'll sit down in a minute, mate.

176
00:10:48.483 --> 00:10:49.484
Deep breaths, mate.

177
00:10:50.610 --> 00:10:52.404
-Rebecca.
-Sam.

178
00:10:52.988 --> 00:10:57.200
And Colin, and Isaac, and Nathan.

179
00:10:57.826 --> 00:11:00.787
Everyone.
Thank you all so much for coming.

180
00:11:00.870 --> 00:11:02.330
I'm sorry for your loss.

181
00:11:02.414 --> 00:11:03.873
Yeah, sorry for your loss.

182
00:11:04.749 --> 00:11:06.001
Yes--

183
00:11:07.085 --> 00:11:10.505
Fathers are the training wheels
on the bikes of…

184
00:11:14.175 --> 00:11:17.053
Sorry-- I just didn't want to say
what they said, so I--

185
00:11:17.637 --> 00:11:18.722
Sorry for your loss.

186
00:11:37.115 --> 00:11:38.158
Sassy.

187
00:11:38.742 --> 00:11:41.119
Oh, decrepit shitbag.

188
00:11:41.202 --> 00:11:45.248
Oh, come on, Sass.
Let's let bygones be bygones, eh?

189
00:11:45.332 --> 00:11:48.084
I've got a daughter now. I've changed.

190
00:11:48.168 --> 00:11:49.419
Oh, right.

191
00:11:50.003 --> 00:11:51.755
Having a daughter erases

192
00:11:51.838 --> 00:11:54.925
all the shitty things
you've done to women in your lifetime.

193
00:11:55.008 --> 00:11:56.051
Cool.

194
00:11:56.885 --> 00:12:02.349
Rupert,
I think about your death every single day.

195
00:12:03.016 --> 00:12:04.017
I can't wait.

196
00:12:05.227 --> 00:12:07.437
I'm gonna wear red to your funeral.

197
00:12:08.063 --> 00:12:12.984
I will be a beacon of joy
to the other three people there.

198
00:12:15.195 --> 00:12:16.446
Always a pleasure, Sassy.

199
00:12:16.529 --> 00:12:18.657
Fuck off and die, Rupert.

200
00:12:28.291 --> 00:12:29.626
Good morning, Ted.

201
00:12:33.004 --> 00:12:34.172
Okay.

202
00:12:35.298 --> 00:12:38.343
Ted, you're-- Ted, you're okay.

203
00:12:38.426 --> 00:12:39.928
Just breathe.

204
00:12:40.679 --> 00:12:43.306
Just focus on your 4-7-8 breathing.

205
00:12:45.058 --> 00:12:47.394
You can. Come on. Just breathe.

206
00:12:47.477 --> 00:12:48.937
I'm on my way.

207
00:12:59.197 --> 00:13:00.282
That baby sucks.

208
00:13:01.366 --> 00:13:03.159
You don't have to say that for me.

209
00:13:03.243 --> 00:13:04.828
I'm not just saying it. I'm serious.

210
00:13:05.787 --> 00:13:08.039
That baby's whack. I hate it.

211
00:13:09.499 --> 00:13:11.793
-I love you.
-I love you too.

212
00:13:12.919 --> 00:13:15.046
-I'm here for you, whatever you need.
-I know.

213
00:13:16.131 --> 00:13:17.424
I won't leave your side.

214
00:13:18.008 --> 00:13:21.678
-Jones!
-Sassy! Oh, my God!

215
00:13:23.513 --> 00:13:25.015
Hi!

216
00:13:26.683 --> 00:13:27.893
I'm used to it.

217
00:13:28.810 --> 00:13:30.061
Sorry for your loss.

218
00:13:30.729 --> 00:13:33.773
-You look amazing!
-Good to see you. Thank you.

219
00:13:33.857 --> 00:13:35.692
You're fine. Keep walking.

220
00:13:35.775 --> 00:13:36.985
God.

221
00:13:37.652 --> 00:13:39.070
I guess we're supposed to be sad.

222
00:13:39.154 --> 00:13:40.906
Yeah, yeah.

223
00:13:40.989 --> 00:13:42.699
Funerals are so weird.

224
00:13:42.782 --> 00:13:45.285
I was literally talking about
that earlier.

225
00:13:45.785 --> 00:13:48.663
-Do you also wanna be a tree when you die?
-Hell yeah.

226
00:13:48.747 --> 00:13:50.665
Or a really stupid dog.

227
00:13:51.791 --> 00:13:53.251
Either one is a great life.

228
00:13:54.169 --> 00:13:55.212
Yeah.

229
00:13:55.295 --> 00:13:56.546
So where's Ted?

230
00:13:57.464 --> 00:13:59.925
-Sassy and Ted, sitting in a tree.
-Oh, God.

231
00:14:00.008 --> 00:14:03.470
-F-U-C-K-I-N-G.
-Shut up, you little troll.

232
00:14:04.638 --> 00:14:07.849
I'm sorry.
I say mean things to beautiful women.

233
00:14:07.933 --> 00:14:09.517
Thanks, Sass.

234
00:14:10.936 --> 00:14:12.896
By the way, record scratch,

235
00:14:12.979 --> 00:14:15.357
but I think Rebecca is
secretly dating someone.

236
00:14:15.440 --> 00:14:17.025
-What?
-For, like, weeks.

237
00:14:17.609 --> 00:14:19.653
Now, is today an inappropriate day

238
00:14:19.736 --> 00:14:23.114
to inquire/badger her into telling us who?

239
00:14:23.865 --> 00:14:25.450
We'll never know unless we try.

240
00:14:31.748 --> 00:14:33.291
-Keeley.
-Jamie.

241
00:14:33.792 --> 00:14:35.168
Wow, nice suit.

242
00:14:36.169 --> 00:14:37.629
All of you. Look at you.

243
00:14:40.131 --> 00:14:42.300
Look. Hey. Come here.

244
00:14:42.384 --> 00:14:44.594
Is this--
Is this the suit that Ted got you?

245
00:14:45.178 --> 00:14:46.429
-What, this?
-Yeah.

246
00:14:47.347 --> 00:14:48.557
I can't remember--

247
00:14:48.640 --> 00:14:50.809
Yes. Yeah, yeah.

248
00:14:50.892 --> 00:14:52.269
Yeah, it's-- Yeah.

249
00:14:52.352 --> 00:14:53.937
-Nice, it's really nice.
-Thank you.

250
00:14:54.020 --> 00:14:57.065
Another man buying you clothes
is infantilizing, yes?

251
00:15:00.569 --> 00:15:02.028
Fuck's sake.

252
00:15:03.029 --> 00:15:06.366
Well, no.
He doesn't buy all of my clothes.

253
00:15:06.449 --> 00:15:08.535
Most of them are gifts from my mum.
You know.

254
00:15:10.161 --> 00:15:11.496
Let's go.

255
00:15:16.877 --> 00:15:18.211
Is that a fucking apple?

256
00:15:18.295 --> 00:15:19.296
Yeah.

257
00:15:20.255 --> 00:15:21.923
I got it from a tree outside.

258
00:15:22.507 --> 00:15:23.884
Tastes like dead people.

259
00:15:23.967 --> 00:15:25.886
That's not funny, Roy.

260
00:15:25.969 --> 00:15:29.222
No, but it's surprisingly delicious.

261
00:15:32.851 --> 00:15:35.729
Cheer up, Keeley. It's a funeral.

262
00:15:41.902 --> 00:15:44.195
I hate dress shoes so much, Jamie.

263
00:15:45.697 --> 00:15:47.324
I know, muchacho.

264
00:15:47.407 --> 00:15:49.659
'Cause remember,
they ain't made for people like us.

265
00:15:50.327 --> 00:15:51.661
They're made for sheep.

266
00:15:52.746 --> 00:15:54.664
They're made for Muggles.

267
00:15:55.582 --> 00:15:56.875
They're made for twats.

268
00:15:56.958 --> 00:16:00.754
When I get home, I will set them on fire,
and their memory will burn in hell.

269
00:16:00.837 --> 00:16:02.339
Jesus, Dani.

270
00:16:03.506 --> 00:16:07.010
Jesús has no place in the conversation
of these damn shoes.

271
00:16:43.088 --> 00:16:44.297
How you feeling, Ted?

272
00:16:45.674 --> 00:16:46.800
I'm better, you know?

273
00:16:46.883 --> 00:16:48.218
Not great, but better.

274
00:16:49.010 --> 00:16:50.011
Good.

275
00:16:53.181 --> 00:16:54.474
Because when someone's not great,

276
00:16:54.558 --> 00:16:56.476
that allows me to get in there
and do my thing.

277
00:16:58.019 --> 00:16:59.020
Yeah.

278
00:17:00.855 --> 00:17:02.107
May I sit down?

279
00:17:02.190 --> 00:17:03.733
I wish the doctor would, yeah.

280
00:17:11.157 --> 00:17:13.577
You want something to drink?
A cup of tea or something?

281
00:17:13.660 --> 00:17:16.036
No, thank you. I hate tea.

282
00:17:16.121 --> 00:17:17.622
Tastes like a wet paper bag.

283
00:17:22.459 --> 00:17:23.837
I'll tell you anything.

284
00:17:28.967 --> 00:17:31.845
I don't think I've ever been
in a properly…

285
00:17:31.928 --> 00:17:34.764
Anglican house of worship before, and…

286
00:17:36.141 --> 00:17:39.019
it makes me miss you,
and I just wish you were here.

287
00:17:39.102 --> 00:17:41.813
Me too. I love funerals.

288
00:17:41.897 --> 00:17:43.231
Is it an open casket?

289
00:17:43.315 --> 00:17:45.567
God, I hope so. I like to see.

290
00:17:46.359 --> 00:17:47.360
Me too.

291
00:17:51.823 --> 00:17:53.575
Yeah, yeah. You know what?

292
00:17:55.201 --> 00:17:58.914
-You can't be serious.
-I'm dead serious!

293
00:18:00.081 --> 00:18:01.583
What? I mean it.

294
00:18:01.666 --> 00:18:04.336
When I was a kid, the only thing I liked
about church was confession.

295
00:18:04.419 --> 00:18:05.420
It was so freeing.

296
00:18:05.503 --> 00:18:08.089
I'd just sit there and admit
all the sickest shit inside of my brain.

297
00:18:09.507 --> 00:18:12.886
Oh, my God. One time, I made the priest
blush and barf at the same time.

298
00:18:13.803 --> 00:18:15.138
Yeah.

299
00:18:15.222 --> 00:18:18.433
I have been told to come in
to ask you to lower your voices.

300
00:18:20.060 --> 00:18:21.478
But I also brought this.

301
00:18:21.561 --> 00:18:24.272
-Oh, good work.
-Oh, nice.

302
00:18:24.356 --> 00:18:26.066
Stole it from a little boy
in a white robe.

303
00:18:26.149 --> 00:18:28.026
No, Sass.

304
00:18:28.109 --> 00:18:30.070
So, Stinky.

305
00:18:30.570 --> 00:18:33.907
-Who are you secretly shagging?
-What?

306
00:18:33.990 --> 00:18:36.284
Let's skip the part
where you pretend you're not, yeah?

307
00:18:37.035 --> 00:18:39.079
What are you even talking about?

308
00:18:39.663 --> 00:18:42.207
How about
the bullshit text after the date,

309
00:18:42.290 --> 00:18:45.001
the fact I have not seen you
outside of work for two weeks,

310
00:18:45.835 --> 00:18:47.837
and that even though today is
your father's funeral,

311
00:18:47.921 --> 00:18:50.090
you are glowing like a girl
that just got properly plowed.

312
00:18:50.757 --> 00:18:51.758
God.

313
00:18:53.969 --> 00:18:55.095
Shit.

314
00:18:56.429 --> 00:18:59.683
-I knew it! I knew it!
-Oh, my God! You're right!

315
00:18:59.766 --> 00:19:03.353
I've been asked to come in
and tell you to lower your voices.

316
00:19:03.436 --> 00:19:05.480
The vicar looked like he wanted to swear.

317
00:19:05.564 --> 00:19:06.856
Is everything all right?

318
00:19:06.940 --> 00:19:07.941
Yeah, of course.

319
00:19:08.024 --> 00:19:10.318
We're just trying to figure out
who Rebecca is shagging.

320
00:19:10.402 --> 00:19:11.695
Oh, I know.

321
00:19:12.612 --> 00:19:13.822
And it's good.

322
00:19:13.905 --> 00:19:14.990
Mother.

323
00:19:15.073 --> 00:19:17.158
Come on-- Hang on. Hang on.

324
00:19:17.242 --> 00:19:18.827
Okay, let's play 20 questions.

325
00:19:18.910 --> 00:19:22.038
-Yes! Yes.
-Oh, my-- This is thrilling.

326
00:19:22.122 --> 00:19:23.915
Is he tall?

327
00:19:25.000 --> 00:19:26.001
Yes.

328
00:19:26.585 --> 00:19:29.254
-Is it Sam?
-How the fuck did you know that?

329
00:19:29.963 --> 00:19:32.257
-Oh, my God! I fucking did!
-No!

330
00:19:34.384 --> 00:19:36.261
Excuse me for one moment, please.

331
00:19:37.220 --> 00:19:38.221
What?

332
00:19:39.389 --> 00:19:41.391
-I did!
-Oh, my God!

333
00:19:41.474 --> 00:19:42.601
That's it!

334
00:19:42.684 --> 00:19:43.768
Oh, my Go--

335
00:19:44.436 --> 00:19:46.938
Everyone out except immediate family,
please.

336
00:19:47.022 --> 00:19:48.523
You're so bad.

337
00:19:49.774 --> 00:19:51.151
You are.

338
00:19:54.529 --> 00:19:55.780
Sorry.

339
00:19:56.615 --> 00:19:59.117
Boss-ass bitch.

340
00:20:00.869 --> 00:20:02.162
Forgive me, Father.

341
00:20:04.456 --> 00:20:06.291
Sorry, it's terrible behavior.

342
00:20:12.172 --> 00:20:14.799
Ted, it's not surprising
that you had a panic attack.

343
00:20:15.884 --> 00:20:17.844
It's possible that going to this funeral

344
00:20:17.928 --> 00:20:20.597
would trigger memories of going to
your own father's funeral.

345
00:20:22.766 --> 00:20:24.059
Nope. Nope, nope.

346
00:20:24.142 --> 00:20:25.769
I didn't go to my dad's funeral.

347
00:20:26.269 --> 00:20:27.646
Okay, why not?

348
00:20:28.230 --> 00:20:29.481
'Cause he quit.

349
00:20:31.942 --> 00:20:33.360
You know, he quit on his family.

350
00:20:34.653 --> 00:20:36.029
He quit on himself.

351
00:20:38.531 --> 00:20:41.701
And I hated him for that.

352
00:20:45.455 --> 00:20:47.207
I think I still hate him for it.

353
00:20:50.043 --> 00:20:51.419
I think you do too, Ted.

354
00:20:54.589 --> 00:20:55.924
And that's okay.

355
00:20:56.841 --> 00:20:58.301
What happened with your father is

356
00:20:58.385 --> 00:21:01.179
a difficult thing
for anyone to make sense of,

357
00:21:01.263 --> 00:21:03.139
especially his teenage son.

358
00:21:09.145 --> 00:21:10.397
Do you agree?

359
00:21:13.775 --> 00:21:14.901
Yeah, okay.

360
00:21:15.527 --> 00:21:16.653
Okay, good.

361
00:21:17.988 --> 00:21:20.031
Why don't you share with me what happened?

362
00:21:31.918 --> 00:21:33.879
Do you know
what you're going to say in your eulogy?

363
00:21:35.297 --> 00:21:36.673
I don't want to do a eulogy.

364
00:21:36.756 --> 00:21:37.883
Rebecca.

365
00:21:38.466 --> 00:21:41.511
It would look awful if you didn't say
anything at your own father's funeral.

366
00:21:41.595 --> 00:21:42.762
I don't care.

367
00:21:43.388 --> 00:21:45.181
I've got nothing nice to say.

368
00:21:45.265 --> 00:21:46.516
What's got into you?

369
00:21:46.600 --> 00:21:49.978
He was a good father, a wonderful husband.

370
00:21:51.479 --> 00:21:52.480
Was he?

371
00:21:53.148 --> 00:21:54.399
What are you so angry about?

372
00:21:54.983 --> 00:21:58.028
I don't want to talk about it. Not today.

373
00:21:58.111 --> 00:22:00.030
Stop behaving like a child.

374
00:22:00.655 --> 00:22:02.365
Fine, you really want to know?

375
00:22:02.449 --> 00:22:05.577
Because I am so sick of keeping secrets.

376
00:22:07.537 --> 00:22:11.249
Dad cheated on you, and I saw it.

377
00:22:14.377 --> 00:22:15.462
When you were away,

378
00:22:15.545 --> 00:22:18.340
and I was meant
to be staying the night with Sassy.

379
00:22:19.257 --> 00:22:22.093
I even remember the date.
It was Friday the 13th, 199--

380
00:22:22.177 --> 00:22:23.678
…one, in September.

381
00:22:25.055 --> 00:22:27.849
I remember the date 'cause me
and a bunch of high school buddies

382
00:22:27.933 --> 00:22:31.394
were gonna do a marathon
of all them Jason movies that night.

383
00:22:33.813 --> 00:22:36.650
So I, you know,
came home from school as usual

384
00:22:37.609 --> 00:22:40.403
and went up to my room to…

385
00:22:40.487 --> 00:22:42.739
…nick a bottle of wine
from your drinks cabinet,

386
00:22:43.740 --> 00:22:45.742
and as we opened the door,

387
00:22:45.825 --> 00:22:46.826
I heard--

388
00:22:46.910 --> 00:22:48.036
Bang!

389
00:22:49.120 --> 00:22:51.289
So we went to investigate.

390
00:22:52.249 --> 00:22:54.167
I opened up the door, and…

391
00:22:56.920 --> 00:22:58.088
there he was.

392
00:22:58.713 --> 00:23:05.303
In all his glory with his arse in the air
with Mrs. Reynolds screaming his name.

393
00:23:09.724 --> 00:23:12.102
And Sassy didn't say anything

394
00:23:12.185 --> 00:23:14.062
for the first time in her life,
and I just--

395
00:23:14.145 --> 00:23:17.274
Screamed and choked. Cried.

396
00:23:17.357 --> 00:23:19.734
And he came running after me
in his dressing gown,

397
00:23:19.818 --> 00:23:21.319
begging me to stop, but I just--

398
00:23:21.403 --> 00:23:22.904
Ran upstairs, called 911.

399
00:23:24.864 --> 00:23:28.159
Went to the fridge,
grabbed one of his Coors Lights.

400
00:23:28.243 --> 00:23:29.494
Drank that.

401
00:23:31.580 --> 00:23:34.916
Then I called my mom at work
and let her know she needed to come home.

402
00:23:37.669 --> 00:23:39.671
And the next day, when I came back,

403
00:23:39.754 --> 00:23:42.465
he said nothing about it.

404
00:23:43.800 --> 00:23:47.637
And that is why I'm so fucking angry,
okay?

405
00:23:50.473 --> 00:23:52.225
It's why I've always hated him.

406
00:23:57.022 --> 00:23:58.523
And I still hate him.

407
00:24:00.859 --> 00:24:01.902
I know.

408
00:24:01.985 --> 00:24:03.737
No, you don't know how I feel.

409
00:24:03.820 --> 00:24:07.991
I mean, I know about his cheating.

410
00:24:09.326 --> 00:24:10.493
All of it.

411
00:24:11.161 --> 00:24:12.787
You knew, and you did nothing?

412
00:24:12.871 --> 00:24:15.081
Of course I knew. I know everything.

413
00:24:17.125 --> 00:24:18.418
Then I hate you too.

414
00:24:22.547 --> 00:24:24.883
I hate you
for letting him treat you like that.

415
00:24:28.303 --> 00:24:29.846
I'm sorry that happened to you, Ted.

416
00:24:30.513 --> 00:24:31.723
Yeah, me too.

417
00:24:33.141 --> 00:24:35.268
And I understand
why you're angry with him.

418
00:24:36.978 --> 00:24:38.480
He took a lot away from you.

419
00:24:38.563 --> 00:24:39.773
And my mom.

420
00:24:40.649 --> 00:24:42.567
And your mum, yes.

421
00:24:44.611 --> 00:24:46.029
I'm curious about something.

422
00:24:47.280 --> 00:24:48.865
What was he like?

423
00:24:50.575 --> 00:24:52.160
He was a good man, you know.

424
00:24:53.620 --> 00:24:55.455
Real chatterbox, believe it or not.

425
00:24:57.374 --> 00:25:01.253
Probably could have been a little bit
better listening box at times.

426
00:25:04.673 --> 00:25:06.174
What did you love about him?

427
00:25:11.012 --> 00:25:12.305
Why?

428
00:25:12.389 --> 00:25:14.266
You told me what you hate about him.

429
00:25:14.766 --> 00:25:18.144
I'd love to hear something
you remember that made you feel good.

430
00:25:32.534 --> 00:25:35.954
When I was in fifth or sixth grade,
there was this book called Johnny Tremain,

431
00:25:36.663 --> 00:25:39.541
and our homework for,
like, a month was to read this book.

432
00:25:41.459 --> 00:25:44.921
At the end of the month,
I hadn't read a lick of it, you know.

433
00:25:46.298 --> 00:25:48.300
And we had a test,

434
00:25:48.383 --> 00:25:49.759
big test, like, the next day.

435
00:25:50.302 --> 00:25:52.554
And the night before,
I was anxious as all heck,

436
00:25:52.637 --> 00:25:53.680
and I couldn't sleep,

437
00:25:53.763 --> 00:25:55.765
and my dad starts
getting after me about that.

438
00:25:56.516 --> 00:25:57.934
And I start crying.

439
00:25:58.018 --> 00:26:00.186
And he's like, "Whoa, buddy.
What's wrong? What's wrong?"

440
00:26:00.270 --> 00:26:01.521
And I tell him what's up.

441
00:26:02.689 --> 00:26:04.524
And he says,
"Hey, don't worry about it, okay.

442
00:26:04.608 --> 00:26:06.735
Just go up to your room,
lay your head on your pillow

443
00:26:06.818 --> 00:26:09.279
and think about
something you're looking forward to."

444
00:26:09.362 --> 00:26:10.614
So that's what I did.

445
00:26:11.489 --> 00:26:13.074
Next morning, I wake up,
and he says, "Hey,

446
00:26:13.158 --> 00:26:15.535
you ain't gonna ride your bike to school.
I'm gonna drive you."

447
00:26:15.619 --> 00:26:16.870
And I'm like, "All right."

448
00:26:18.038 --> 00:26:21.917
And on the way to school,
he talks me through the entire book,

449
00:26:22.626 --> 00:26:24.920
like it's a bedtime story or something.

450
00:26:26.129 --> 00:26:28.548
'Cause he stayed up all night,
the whole night,

451
00:26:29.549 --> 00:26:31.009
reading the whole damn thing,

452
00:26:31.676 --> 00:26:35.889
'cause he didn't want his little boy
stressed out over some stupid, silly test.

453
00:26:37.307 --> 00:26:39.392
And I ended up getting an A.

454
00:26:39.476 --> 00:26:40.685
Boom.

455
00:26:45.357 --> 00:26:46.608
He was a good dad.

456
00:26:50.946 --> 00:26:52.697
And I don't think he knew that.

457
00:26:58.119 --> 00:27:00.914
I think if he would've known
how good he was

458
00:27:00.997 --> 00:27:03.750
at stuff he didn't really care about
being good at, he--

459
00:27:04.709 --> 00:27:06.461
I don't think he would've done what he--

460
00:27:10.048 --> 00:27:11.424
And I wish I would've told him.

461
00:27:11.508 --> 00:27:13.343
I wish I would've told him more.

462
00:27:17.806 --> 00:27:19.432
I was just so angry at him.

463
00:27:21.184 --> 00:27:22.435
'Cause he was always going to work

464
00:27:22.519 --> 00:27:24.354
and just out with friends
or something like that,

465
00:27:24.437 --> 00:27:25.772
and then he was gone.

466
00:27:31.278 --> 00:27:34.197
And I knew right then and there that
I was never gonna let anybody get by me

467
00:27:34.281 --> 00:27:37.284
without understanding
they might be hurting inside, you know.

468
00:27:39.077 --> 00:27:40.453
'Cause life, it's hard.

469
00:27:44.207 --> 00:27:45.208
It's real hard.

470
00:27:50.922 --> 00:27:52.215
Thank you, Ted.

471
00:27:57.721 --> 00:28:00.015
I don't know
if this is illegal or something,

472
00:28:00.098 --> 00:28:01.141
but can I have a hug?

473
00:28:01.725 --> 00:28:02.726
Sure.

474
00:28:09.441 --> 00:28:10.817
It's okay.

475
00:28:11.401 --> 00:28:13.111
Are you going to charge me
for this session?

476
00:28:14.362 --> 00:28:15.363
Of course I am.

477
00:28:15.447 --> 00:28:17.240
-Okay.
-For the house call.

478
00:28:17.324 --> 00:28:18.658
I appreciate your integrity.

479
00:28:19.242 --> 00:28:20.619
You're welcome.

480
00:28:26.166 --> 00:28:27.334
I'm sorry, Rebecca, but--

481
00:28:29.961 --> 00:28:31.254
I'm not as strong as you.

482
00:28:32.756 --> 00:28:35.175
I was too scared to leave him for good.

483
00:28:35.258 --> 00:28:37.886
You don't think
I was scared leaving Rupert?

484
00:28:39.054 --> 00:28:40.513
I was terrified.

485
00:28:41.056 --> 00:28:43.683
And rightly so because let me tell you,
being alone

486
00:28:44.434 --> 00:28:46.019
is fucking horrible.

487
00:28:48.521 --> 00:28:50.190
But it's been necessary.

488
00:28:54.986 --> 00:28:57.656
'Cause it's actually started
to feel rather wonderful.

489
00:29:00.408 --> 00:29:01.660
Well, I'm glad to hear that.

490
00:29:04.329 --> 00:29:06.706
Besides, Rupert was a self-righteous shit.

491
00:29:07.457 --> 00:29:09.209
Then why are you always so nice to him?

492
00:29:09.292 --> 00:29:11.920
Because, my darling,
the best way to deal with people like that

493
00:29:12.003 --> 00:29:14.422
is to make sure
they know they can't get to you.

494
00:29:15.298 --> 00:29:17.592
Anyway, when all's said and done,

495
00:29:18.343 --> 00:29:22.013
what's more important,
being loving or being right?

496
00:29:24.099 --> 00:29:26.393
I was so proud of you when you left him.

497
00:29:27.644 --> 00:29:29.229
You knew you deserved better.

498
00:29:32.148 --> 00:29:34.067
Now, I've got a whole lot of baggage,

499
00:29:34.943 --> 00:29:37.320
but when I love something,
I love it forever.

500
00:29:37.404 --> 00:29:38.822
And I loved your father.

501
00:29:40.198 --> 00:29:41.825
Even though he treated you like that?

502
00:29:41.908 --> 00:29:42.909
Yeah.

503
00:29:44.327 --> 00:29:46.037
He wasn't perfect.
I didn't need him to be.

504
00:29:46.121 --> 00:29:47.122
He always came back.

505
00:29:51.126 --> 00:29:53.545
You know, I'm actually glad
to hear that you hate me.

506
00:29:55.005 --> 00:29:58.925
All these years, I've thought
you didn't feel anything for me.

507
00:30:00.927 --> 00:30:03.638
I'll take your anger
over your indifference any day.

508
00:30:08.351 --> 00:30:09.352
It's time.

509
00:30:10.020 --> 00:30:12.522
And thank you
for keeping your voices down.

510
00:30:18.695 --> 00:30:19.696
Come on, then.

511
00:30:30.999 --> 00:30:32.542
Let us pray.

512
00:30:34.794 --> 00:30:36.504
Our Father…

513
00:30:36.588 --> 00:30:40.592
…who art in heaven, hallowed be thy name.

514
00:30:41.218 --> 00:30:45.722
Amazing grace

515
00:30:45.805 --> 00:30:49.142
How sweet the sound

516
00:30:49.226 --> 00:30:50.644
"The Lord is my shepherd.

517
00:30:51.228 --> 00:30:53.313
There is nothing I shall want.

518
00:30:53.939 --> 00:30:56.942
Fresh and green are the pastures."

519
00:30:57.025 --> 00:30:58.235
Thank you.

520
